&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m new here and I&amp;rsquo;m also new to type design. Having said that, I&amp;rsquo;ve been drawing type since I was a child and eventually grew up a little and became a graphic designer along the way. My hobby is now taking a serious turn as it&amp;rsquo;s about time I tried to share and even sell my typeface designs. My first attempt was a hand drawn, all caps, neoclassical serif face that I named &amp;lsquo;Carrig&amp;rsquo;. Carrig being the Irish word for &amp;lsquo;rock&amp;rsquo; (I&amp;rsquo;m based in Ireland) and the typeface itself was strongly influenced by classic letterforms carved into stone and weathered by time.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sjiq by Novo Typo</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/100339/</link><pubDate>Mon, 04 Feb 2013 07:16:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/100339/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Sjiq, a new typeface by Novo Typo – (type)designers from Amsterdam, The Netherlands.&lt;br&gt;
